 Bazelisk and repository-download archives still use GitHub caching. Cargo/npm
 downloads and a prebuilt tool image are separate from these compiler/action
 caches; this does not make every Actions cache host-local.
+
+
+## Optional persistent Bazel disk cache
+
+`garm-bazel-disk.nix` defines the additional `runner-zpl-comparison` profile.
+It retains the existing 4 CPU / 8 GiB / 40 GiB VM sizing and networking, and
+shares `/var/lib/garm-bazel-disk/zpl-comparison` into fresh VMs at
+`/var/cache/bazel-persistent`. Incus uses a filesystem share (virtiofs when
+available), so deleting a VM leaves the host directory intact. This directory
+is independent of the existing authenticated remote cache on port 9443.
+The default `runner` profile and existing GARM scale-set selection are unchanged.
+
+The guest cache directory is writable by the current Ubuntu runner UID 1000.
+The comparison workflow checks that the guest path is a mount before enabling
+`--disk_cache=/var/cache/bazel-persistent/zpl-comparison/actions`, with Bazel
+idle garbage collection configured for 40 GB and 14 days. These are GC targets,
+not a filesystem quota. The HTTP remote cache retains its separate 80 GiB limit.
+Warbler must not run the BuildBuddy configuration helper or receive its API key.
+
+A shared writable disk cache is a trust boundary: the remote cache's read-only
+credential does not prevent a job from poisoning this separate disk cache.
+Only select this profile for jobs with the same trust level. Do not attach it
+to a scale set that mixes untrusted pull requests with trusted publication jobs.
+Before production rollout, split runner scheduling/access by trust domain or
+keep untrusted jobs on the existing disposable `runner` profile. A workflow
+label or a directory name alone does not enforce that separation.
+
+After the trust boundary is enforced and the configuration is built/activated,
+select this profile for the comparison scale set using `sudo sys garm scaleset
+update 2 --flavor runner-zpl-comparison`. Verify the effective Incus device and
+runner UID before dispatching a build. Revert that scale set to `--flavor runner`
+to stop attaching the disk; this does not delete cached data.
+
+Validate persistence with two sequential jobs in different VMs: build a small
+Bazel target in the first, then build it in the second with a fresh output base
+and `--remote_cache=`. The second must report a disk-cache hit. Merely seeing
+an existing directory or a hit from the HTTP remote cache is insufficient.
+Run the full timing comparison only after this check passes.
